    "narrative": "Today\u2019s 5x5 Roto slate for the **Austin Waves** presents a couple of intriguing lineup decisions, with **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio** holding down the primary catcher and second base spots respectively.\n\nOur strongest play of the day, despite a pending lineup, is **Liam Hicks**. His raw score of 53.91 is boosted significantly by a dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed Shawn Armstrong and a solid projected batting order slot of #4. The combination of these factors pushes him comfortably into the \"Strong Start\" range. **Brayan Rocchio**, while also benefiting from a favorable SP_xERA projection on Nick Martinez (4.63), sits at the bottom of the lineup (assumed #9) which caps his upside, resulting in a score of 47.20. This places him as a marginal start, one to keep an eye on as the official lineup is confirmed.\n\nLooking at the bench, **Jacob Wilson** narrowly missed the cut, with his score of 55.87 being edged out by **Liam Hicks**' stronger platoon edge. Wilson\u2019s raw projection was excellent, but the specific matchup dynamics for Hicks, particularly the platoon advantage, were the deciding factors. It\u2019s worth noting that **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are all unavailable due to team off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the Injured List and is not an option. We must also be mindful of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio**, as confirmed batting orders could shift their effectiveness.",
